  {"date": "2004-04-16", "venue": "Thomas & Mack Center", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 8, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Hold Your Head Up", "in": ">", "next": "Lifeboy", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2004-06-20", "venue": "Saratoga Performing Arts Center", "city": "Saratoga Springs", "state": "NY", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Although the jam between verses is standard \"Waves\" fare, the band moves into an excellent 7 minute plus jam following the final verse that is rhythmic and upbeat, with multiple movements and \"Maze\" teases.", "prev": "Bill Bailey, Won't You Please Come Home?", "next": "Gumbo", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2004-08-11", "venue": "Tweeter Center", "city": "Mansfield", "state": "MA", "gap": 7, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "One of the best played standard versions of 2.0.", "out": ">", "prev": "Golgi Apparatus", "in": ">", "next": "Tweezer", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2009-06-10", "venue": "Thompson-Boling Arena", "city": "Knoxville", "state": "TN", "gap": 13, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "This is a very well-played version with a full length \"Waves\" jam. 3 minute outro jam leads to transition to \"ASIHTOS.\"", "out": ">", "prev": "Back on the Train", "next": "A Song I Heard the Ocean Sing", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2009-06-20", "venue": "Alpine Valley Music Theatre", "city": "East Troy", "state": "WI", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Sample in a Jar", "xprev": "Run Like an Antelope", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2009-08-02", "venue": "Red Rocks Amphitheatre", "city": "Morrison", "state": "CO", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "note": "Bill Kreutzmann on drums.", "out": ">", "prev": "Also Sprach Zarathustra", "in": ">", "next": "Character Zero", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2011-05-26", "venue": "Bethel Woods Center for the Arts", "city": "Bethel", "state": "NY", "gap": null, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "First played during Superball IX's From the Archives show and later released as LP on LP 02, this tech rehearsal version of \"Waves\" represented a turning point of 3.0 by proving beyond a shadow of a doubt that Phish was still capable of astounding long-form improv. Elements that would reappear in key moments of 2011 such as the \"A Love Supreme\" theme in the 6/3/11 DWD and the abstract transcendence of the 7/2/11 Storage Jam are also present, further underscoring the outsized influence of this momentous performance. The FTA track begins with Trey asking Page \"Do you want to play a jammier song?\" to which Page replies \"Sure, I do\", and what resulted stands as one of the finest jams of any era. Departing the song at 7:45 with a willingness to explore and employing a wide array of tones and textures, the band charts a course for choppy waters and intentional discord enhanced by Trey's \"out\" playing. From the depths of the churning storm, an exquisite final movement of immense beauty eventually emerges to bring this odyssey of improvisation to a conclusion that is all at once wistful, cathartic, and profound.", "first": 1, "last": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2011-05-27", "venue": "Bethel Woods Center for the Arts", "city": "Bethel", "state": "NY", "gap": 77, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Fantastic playing by Trey in the jam proper. Beautiful, lush and serene outro jam. In many ways the polar opposite of the haunting outro from \"IT.\" Transitions to a solid \"Prince Caspian.\"", "out": ">", "prev": "Boogie On Reggae Woman", "in": ">", "next": "Prince Caspian", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2011-06-11", "venue": "Merriweather Post Pavilion", "city": "Columbia", "state": "MD", "gap": 10, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Silent in the Morning", "in": ">", "next": "Chalk Dust Torture", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2011-07-03", "venue": "Watkins Glen International", "city": "Watkins Glen", "state": "NY", "gap": 8, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Light", "next": "What's the Use?", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2011-08-15", "venue": "UIC Pavilion, University of Illinois", "city": "Chicago", "state": "IL", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "\"Waves\" jam is intense and good, but following the final verse, the band breaks into a nice, snappy rocking jam that segues -> masterfully into \"Undermind.\"", "out": "->", "prev": "Dirt", "in": ">", "next": "Undermind", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2012-06-28", "venue": "Klipsch Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 21, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Delicate and beautifully played at first, the jam has growing intensity, and then leaves the \"Waves\" ranch altogether with several movements that skirt around the perimeter of \"Waves\" proper. Unfinished with > to \"Bug.\"", "out": ">", "prev": "Prince Caspian", "in": ">", "next": "Bug", "nb": 1},
